# After opening a pull request

Every time you open a PR (`gh pr create` or equivalent), immediately run the
setup script against the PR you just created, from the repo root:

```bash
.cursor/scripts/pr-setup.sh <pr-url>
```

The script assigns `@me` to the PR, adds it to the `Gamaliel Roadmap` project
(org `gamaliel-ai`, project number 1), sets Status to **In progress**, sets
Sprint to whichever iteration covers today, and sets **Project Start date**
to today.

Run it as a separate command after `gh pr create` returns, so a failure in the
setup step never hides the PR URL. Report the PR URL and the sprint it landed in.

If the script fails with a missing-scope error, the fix is
`gh auth refresh -h github.com -s project,read:project`. Tell the user to run
that rather than working around it.
